  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">OneManifold</rdfs:label>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A topological space with the property that each point has a neighborhood that is homeomorphic to an open subset of 1-dimensional Euclidean space.</rdfs:comment>
  <core:altLabel xml:lang="en">1-manifold</core:altLabel>
  <core:prefLabel xml:lang="en">OneManifold</core:prefLabel>
  <emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">A topological space with the property that each point has a neighborhood that is homeomorphic to an open subset of 1-dimensional Euclidean space.</emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
  <emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f xml:lang="en">One-dimensional manifolds include lines and circles, but not self-crossing curves. Two-dimensional manifolds are also called surfaces. Examples include the plane, the sphere, and the torus, and also the Klein bottle and real projective plane.</emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f>
</owl:Class>

