  <emmo:EMMO_8a137e9f_579c_4e28_baca_e8980eb0c3db rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">disjointUnionOf: Becquerel, Coulomb, DegreeCelsius, Farad, Gray, Henry, Hertz, Joule, Katal, Lumen, Lux, Newton, Ohm, Pascal, Radian, Siemens, Sievert, Steradian, Tesla, Volt, Watt, Weber</emmo:EMMO_8a137e9f_579c_4e28_baca_e8980eb0c3db>
  <emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">The 22 derived units that are given a special name in the SI system that stands for units derived by SI base units.</emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
  <emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f xml:lang="en">These units are SI coherent by definition.</emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f>
  <emmo:EMMO_c84c6752_6d64_48cc_9500_e54a3c34898d rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_System_of_Units#Derived_units</emmo:EMMO_c84c6752_6d64_48cc_9500_e54a3c34898d>
</owl:Class>

<owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/emmo#Lumen">
  <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/units/siunits#"/>
  <rdfs:subClassOf>
    <owl:Restriction>
      <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_daf7a9b7_18ef_4e73_9fb9_75adfd9800e8"/>
      <owl:hasValue rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">lm</owl:hasValue>
    </owl:Restriction>
  </rdfs:subClassOf>
  <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_0266ec8c_bd13_4c9c_be77_607498793ed3"/>
  <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_14ff4393_0f28_4fb4_abc7_c2cc00bc761d"/>
  <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_1abe0ea7_2378_402f_b950_89b0795d2f45"/>
  <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_9e5f464a_658c_4b34_b80d_a5f8d5ec811a"/>
  <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_e9ffc696_5228_4ff9_8a60_0f5e05e9931b"/>
  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Lumen</rdfs:label>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">SI unit for luminous flux.</rdfs:comment>
  <core:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Lumen</core:prefLabel>
  <sche:unitCode rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">LUM</sche:unitCode>
  <emmo:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/LM</emmo:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc>
  <emmo:EMMO_33ae2d07_5526_4555_a0b4_8f4c031b5652 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">lm</emmo:EMMO_33ae2d07_5526_4555_a0b4_8f4c031b5652>
  <emmo:EMMO_6dd685dd_1895_46e4_b227_be9f7d643c25 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">http://dbpedia.org/resource/Lumen</emmo:EMMO_6dd685dd_1895_46e4_b227_be9f7d643c25>
  <emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">SI unit for luminous flux.</emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
  <emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f xml:lang="en">The SI unit for measuring the flux of light being produced by a light source or received by a surface. The intensity of a light source is measured in candelas. One lumen represents the total flux of light emitted, equal to the intensity in candelas multiplied by the solid angle in steradians into which the light is emitted. A full sphere has a solid angle of 4·π steradians. A light source that uniformly radiates one candela in all directions has a total luminous flux of 1 cd·4π sr = 4π cd·sr ≈ 12.57 lumens. "Lumen" is a Latin word for light.

-- QUDT</emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f>
