  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Equation</rdfs:label>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An equation with variables can always be represented as:

f(v0, v1, ..., vn) = g(v0, v1, ..., vn)

where f is the left hand and g the right hand  side expressions and v0, v1, ..., vn are the variables.</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The class of 'mathematical'-s that stand for a statement of equality between two mathematical expressions.</rdfs:comment>
  <core:example xml:lang="en">2+3 = 5
x^2 +3x  = 5x
dv/dt = a
sin(x) = y</core:example>
  <core:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Equation</core:prefLabel>
  <emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">The class of 'mathematical'-s that stand for a statement of equality between two mathematical expressions.</emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
</owl:Class>

