<owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/emmo#StatvoltPerCentiMetre">
  <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/units/unclassifiedunits#"/>
  <rdfs:subClassOf>
    <owl:Restriction>
      <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_d088a3cb_d3e3_4eb2_9897_00aef0cb00cd"/>
      <owl:hasValue rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double">0.0</owl:hasValue>
    </owl:Restriction>
  </rdfs:subClassOf>
  <rdfs:subClassOf>
    <owl:Restriction>
      <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_8189b42e_0995_423a_a26c_51168b27c3cf"/>
      <owl:hasValue rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double">29979.25</owl:hasValue>
    </owl:Restriction>
  </rdfs:subClassOf>
  <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_8246541a_f1f6_4d03_8bd7_fc6b76d17375"/>
  <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_c6d4a5e0_7e95_44df_a6db_84ee0a8bbc8e"/>
  <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_ebf9a5c6_ca80_45d4_a991_24a1bf4b6720"/>
  <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">StatvoltPerCentiMetre</rdfs:label>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">One statvolt per centimetre is equal in magnitude to one gauss. For example, an electric field of one statvolt/cm has the same energy density as a magnetic field of one gauss. Likewise, a plane wave propagating in a vacuum has perpendicular electric and magnetic fields such that for every gauss of magnetic field intensity there is one statvolt/cm of electric field intensity.
The abvolt is another option for a unit of voltage in the cgs system.

-- QUDT</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/2.1/vocab/unit</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
  <core:altLabel xml:lang="en">Statvolt per Centimetre</core:altLabel>
  <core:prefLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">StatvoltPerCentiMetre</core:prefLabel>
  <emmo:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/V_Stat-PER-CentiM</emmo:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc>
  <emmo:EMMO_7f1dec83_d85e_4e1b_b7bd_c9442d4f5a64 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">statV/cm</emmo:EMMO_7f1dec83_d85e_4e1b_b7bd_c9442d4f5a64>
  <emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">One statvolt per centimetre is equal in magnitude to one gauss. For example, an electric field of one statvolt/cm has the same energy density as a magnetic field of one gauss. Likewise, a plane wave propagating in a vacuum has perpendicular electric and magnetic fields such that for every gauss of magnetic field intensity there is one statvolt/cm of electric field intensity.
The abvolt is another option for a unit of voltage in the cgs system.

-- QUDT</emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
  <emmo:EMMO_c84c6752_6d64_48cc_9500_e54a3c34898d rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Statvolt</emmo:EMMO_c84c6752_6d64_48cc_9500_e54a3c34898d>
</owl:Class>

