  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">MagneticDipoleMoment</rdfs:label>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">For an atom or nucleus, this energy is quantized and can be written as:

    W = g μ M B

where g is the appropriate g factor, μ is mostly the Bohr magneton or nuclear magneton, M is magnetic quantum number, and B is magnitude of the magnetic flux density.

-- ISO 80000</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Vector quantity μ causing a change to its energy ΔW in an external magnetic field of field flux density B:

    ΔW = −μ · B</rdfs:comment>
  <core:prefLabel xml:lang="en">MagneticDipoleMoment</core:prefLabel>
  <emmo:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/MagneticDipoleMoment</emmo:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc>
  <emmo:EMMO_50c298c2_55a2_4068_b3ac_4e948c33181f rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">https://www.electropedia.org/iev/iev.nsf/display?openform&amp;ievref=121-11-55</emmo:EMMO_50c298c2_55a2_4068_b3ac_4e948c33181f>
