  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">USPerm</rdfs:label>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A perm is a unit of permeance or "water vapor transmission" given a certain differential in partial pressures on either side of a material or membrane. The U.S. perm is defined as 1 grain of water vapor per hour, per square foot, per inch of mercury.

-- QUDT</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/2.1/vocab/unit</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
