  <emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">A perm is a unit of permeance or "water vapor transmission" given a certain differential in partial pressures on either side of a material or membrane. The U.S. perm is defined as 1 grain of water vapor per hour, per square foot, per inch of mercury.

