<owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/emmo#Fathom">
  <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/units/unclassifiedunits#"/>
  <rdfs:subClassOf>
    <owl:Restriction>
      <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_8189b42e_0995_423a_a26c_51168b27c3cf"/>
      <owl:hasValue rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double">1.8288</owl:hasValue>
    </owl:Restriction>
  </rdfs:subClassOf>
  <rdfs:subClassOf>
    <owl:Restriction>
      <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_d088a3cb_d3e3_4eb2_9897_00aef0cb00cd"/>
      <owl:hasValue rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double">0.0</owl:hasValue>
    </owl:Restriction>
  </rdfs:subClassOf>
  <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_8246541a_f1f6_4d03_8bd7_fc6b76d17375"/>
  <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_868ae137_4d25_493e_b270_21ea3d94849e"/>
  <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_b3600e73_3e05_479d_9714_c041c3acf5cc"/>
  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Fathom</rdfs:label>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A fathom = 1.8288 meters, is a unit of length in the imperial and the U.S. customary systems, used especially for measuring the depth of water. There are two yards in an imperial or U.S. fathom. Originally based on the distance between the man's outstretched arms, the size of a fathom has varied slightly depending on whether it was defined as a thousandth of an (Admiralty) nautical mile or as a multiple of the imperial yard.  Abbreviations: f, fath, fm, fth, fthm.

-- QUDT</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/2.1/vocab/unit</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
  <core:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Fathom</core:prefLabel>
  <emmo:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/FATH</emmo:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc>
  <emmo:EMMO_33ae2d07_5526_4555_a0b4_8f4c031b5652 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">[fth_i]</emmo:EMMO_33ae2d07_5526_4555_a0b4_8f4c031b5652>
  <emmo:EMMO_7f1dec83_d85e_4e1b_b7bd_c9442d4f5a64 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">fathom</emmo:EMMO_7f1dec83_d85e_4e1b_b7bd_c9442d4f5a64>
  <emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">A fathom = 1.8288 meters, is a unit of length in the imperial and the U.S. customary systems, used especially for measuring the depth of water. There are two yards in an imperial or U.S. fathom. Originally based on the distance between the man's outstretched arms, the size of a fathom has varied slightly depending on whether it was defined as a thousandth of an (Admiralty) nautical mile or as a multiple of the imperial yard.  Abbreviations: f, fath, fm, fth, fthm.

-- QUDT</emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
  <emmo:EMMO_c84c6752_6d64_48cc_9500_e54a3c34898d rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fathom?oldid=493265429</emmo:EMMO_c84c6752_6d64_48cc_9500_e54a3c34898d>
</owl:Class>

