  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">StatcoulombPerMole</rdfs:label>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">"Statcoulomb per Mole" is a unit of measure for the electical charge associated with one mole of a substance. The mole is a unit of measurement used in chemistry to express amounts of a chemical substance, defined as an amount of a substance that contains as many elementary entities (e.g., atoms, molecules, ions, electrons) as there are atoms in 12 grams of pure carbon-12 (12C), the isotope of carbon with atomic weight 12.

-- QUDT</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/2.1/vocab/unit</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
  <core:altLabel xml:lang="en">Statcoulomb per Mole</core:altLabel>
